{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1023864-limits-on-sustaining-locking-and-other-preparation","id":1023864,"title":"Limits on Sustaining, Locking and other preparation?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-29T11:21:41-08:00","id":1023864,"title":"Limits on Sustaining, Locking and other preparation?","content":"So, in preparation for running a M20 game, it occurred to me that while there is a huge difference between a rival mage that is prepared and one that isn't (obviously), there isn't any mention about how much preparation that a typical mage would have under different conditions. So, for those that run Mage games, how do you determine how much preparation (and the game effects thereof)?<br /> <br /> For Sustaining effects, since those are locked to the location / scene that they were cast in, those wouldn't come into play unless the scene is at the antagonist's home/lair/safe house. But if they are, we can still work with the notion that since every 2 sustained effects, starting at 3rd, adds a +1 TN to future castings, there would probably only be 1-2 (for +0 TN) or 3-4 (for +1).<br /> <br /> But as for Locking effects (like the extra-armor trench coat), aside from the actual process of rolling the dice and checking for Paradox, is there a reasonable limit on how many effects can be locked at once? And that question goes for effects locked onto a single specific target and, separately, for all locked effects, total. I ask because aside from running the risk of the dice and Paradox, it doesn't seem to be either a hard or soft limit.<br /> <br /> Likewise, how do those of you that run games determine the potency of these preparation effects (i.e. how many successes the rival mage has achieved in preparation)? Do people actually roll the ritual casting off scene and hope the Big Bad doesn't blow themselves up with 'Dox before the party gets to the showdown?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12655,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12655-tzizimine","user":"tzizimine","date":". 12-29-2016, 03:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12655-tzizimine","name":"tzizimine","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T12:46:27-08:00","id":1023898,"title":"","content":"Personally, I never roll NPC spells unless if failure is an option. If you're setting up a final battle, how anticlimactic would it be for the players if the big boss blew themselves up before they got a chance to do anything?<br /> Thin about what they would do in preparation, and how you expect your players to deal with them. And don't be afraid to add effects after the fact to deal with things if it's logically conceivable that they would have prepare for something that you yourself did not anticipate. You're designing a boss fight, not playing as the antagonist.<br /> <br /> Now, I'm not sure how M20 differs, but the way I've done it is there is no hard limit on how many effects you have running at once, but the more effects you have running, the more difficult it is to do further effects, an let the law of diminishing returns take hold from there.<br /> <br /> It doesn't matter if it's locked or not, all effects add up to the difficulty, and if your players are anything like mine, this will be big enough a deterrent on its own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 12-29-2016, 06:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T12:56:53-08:00","id":1023902,"title":"","content":"You also need to be careful about the difficulty increase for every 2 effects with M20, as it explicitely states that it does not apply to effects that are locked onto a pattern, nor to effects that the Mage does not have to actively focus/concentrate on.<br /> <br /> So, if the mage wants to levitate an object while also trying to actively fend off a mind attack, those definitely count. However, having enhanced perceptions while having a warming effects locked onto your pattern and also having having a piece of clothing that has a locked matter effect to make it bulletproof, none of those count against the limit. Effectively any effects the Mage has to pay attention to, count. Those that are fire-and-forget don't.<br /> <br /> Another thing M20 allows you, is sustain an effect after its duration has passed...by making it count against the difficulty increase limit from then on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T13:15:13-08:00","id":1023911,"title":"","content":"Recently in my games I've begun allowing locked effects. I found them a bit overpowering since it bypasses the difficulty modifiers for every 2 effects. <br /> <br /> I balanced this by requiring the sphere level needed to lock the effect be that which would allow a major transformation. Which does fit with HDYDT's requirements. Life 4, Matter 2, Spirit 4, and Entropy 3 or 4 depending on the nature of the target (matter or life). I also require 1 point of quintessence to lock the effect for the duration, which may be permanent if enough successes are occured to do so. This of course is the real limiting factor until you have characters with Prime 4+, but by then their opponents are equally prepared. So far its working fine even though I do have a Choruser with the talisman from Forged by Dragons Fire that destroys objects for quintessence and is a periaphat (spelling). But then the also only have a rank 2 node available to the party of 6 so he is actually their main source of quintessence and he incurs a point of paradox every time he uses it to get 1 point of quintessence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T13:30:48-08:00","id":1023920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1023864-limits-on-sustaining-locking-and-other-preparation?p=1023898#post1023898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I never roll NPC spells unless I failure is an option. I you're setting up a final battle, how anticlimactic would it be for the players if the big boss blew themselves up before they got a chance to do anything?<br /> Thin about what they would do in preparation, and how you expect your players to deal with them. And don't be afraid to add effects after the fact to deal with things if it's logically conceivable that they would have prepare for something that you yourself did not anticipate. You're designing a boss fight, not playing as the antagonist.<br /> <br /> Now, I'm not sure how M20 differs, but the way I've done it is there is no hard limit on how many effects you have running at once, but the more effects you have running, the more difficult it is to do further effects, an let the law of diminishing returns take hold from there.<br /> <br /> It doesn't matter if it's locked or not, all effects add up to the difficulty, and if your players are anything like mine, this will be big enough a deterrent on its own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Saikou, I agree with you that anticlimactic issue. But that raises another question. How do you (and that general specific to Saikou and in general to everyone) determine how many successes the Big Bad gets on effect X if you are not rolling it? Do you use a formula based on Arete and TN? like average successes calculator? Do you assume successes equal to Arete or 1/2 Arete? Single casting vs. ritual? Do you just fudge it, like &quot;Big Bad needs to do this so I am giving X successes. How he gets it / chances of it actually happening don't matter.&quot;?<br /> <br /> And to be clear, I am not looking for RAW vs. RAI or general ideas. I am looking for math. Big Bad X has Y factors, resulting Z successes. In other words, your personal favorite method of determining successes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12655-tzizimine","name":"tzizimine","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T13:45:42-08:00","id":1023931,"title":"","content":"For rituals and extended castings I start with minimum number of successes required then add twice their Arete. I adjust up or down from there or leave it there depending on what I want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T13:49:41-08:00","id":1023933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tuch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1023864-limits-on-sustaining-locking-and-other-preparation?p=1023931#post1023931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For rituals and extended castings I start with minimum number of successes required then add twice their Arete. I adjust up or down from there or leave it there depending on what I want.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks, Tuch","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12655-tzizimine","name":"tzizimine","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T02:34:21-08:00","id":1024170,"title":"","content":"Revised era HR:<br /> Arete+3-TN=successes per roll.<br /> <br /> I made this up for the morning rituals.<br /> You dedicate X time and split it against the desired effects. Standard roll equals 3 minutes. Rituals depend on several factors. Rituals for the sake of omitting the +1 difficulty per added roll take 15 minutes.<br /> <br /> The +3 in the formula are from a HR which gives bonus dice under certain circumstances.<br /> <br /> In M20 the group opted for rolling the dice when the pre-cast effect comes into play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T11:05:19-08:00","id":1024409,"title":"","content":"Wonderful. I assume HR means House Rule. but that is still spot on what I was looking for.<br /> <br /> Also, has anyone discovered a hard or soft limit to number of effects that could be locked? Either to a single object or total?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12655-tzizimine","name":"tzizimine","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T02:06:44-08:00","id":1024674,"title":"","content":"Soft limit?<br /> Disbelief.<br /> It dissolves vulgar stuff given time.<br /> Hard limit is a citizen of Stfiatopolis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T07:12:57-08:00","id":1024747,"title":"","content":"That's what I kind of figured. One of the aspects about class-less RPG systems (WoD, Shadowrun, Fate, etc.) that I have always had a problem with is determining the stats and game mechanics of the opposition for an appropriately challenging fight. D20/Pathfinder has the CR/EL system which, while not perfect by any means, gives at least an idea of a party X powerful can handle Y challenge. Doing the same in a class-less system is a skill I have yet to achieve in my 20+ years of gaming.<br /> <br /> The best method I have found so far is to keep copies of everyone's character and run mock encounters using the average die results and see if anything falls apart in the first few interactions (learned that lesson in a vampire game when it was 1 werewolf against a cotorie where no one had Fortitude. Aggravated damage is/was a huge game changer. 2 True Deaths and 2 more in torpor for weeks).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12655-tzizimine","name":"tzizimine","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T08:29:11-08:00","id":1024768,"title":"","content":"Since it is part of the name (Storytelling) I cheat, a lot.<br /> In both directions.<br /> If you're in a game of reality bending you can pretty much go all the way. Nothing is set in stone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T08:39:11-08:00","id":1024772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tzizimine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1023864-limits-on-sustaining-locking-and-other-preparation?p=1024747#post1024747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's what I kind of figured. One of the aspects about class-less RPG systems (WoD, Shadowrun, Fate, etc.) that I have always had a problem with is determining the stats and game mechanics of the opposition for an appropriately challenging fight. D20/Pathfinder has the CR/EL system which, while not perfect by any means, gives at least an idea of a party X powerful can handle Y challenge. Doing the same in a class-less system is a skill I have yet to achieve in my 20+ years of gaming.<br /> <br /> The best method I have found so far is to keep copies of everyone's character and run mock encounters using the average die results and see if anything falls apart in the first few interactions (learned that lesson in a vampire game when it was 1 werewolf against a cotorie where no one had Fortitude. Aggravated damage is/was a huge game changer. 2 True Deaths and 2 more in torpor for weeks).</div> </div> </div> </div>You may not like my way of doing things, but I don't really worry about fully stating up my NPCs. For important ones, I might note down what spheres I expect them to all have, their arete level, and maybe their attributes, just so I keep a little consistency, but that's about it. Everything else is really free-form.<br /> For example, when my players are fighting spirits, I'll have a few spirits prepared, and just throw 2 at them and see how they get on. If they're having a lot of trouble with them, then I'll leave it at that. If they seem to tear through them pretty easily, I'll add a couple more mid-battle.<br /> <br /> The same thing can be done with the NWO Blacksuits, Progentior Clones/Victors, Demons, Nephandic goons, thugs, what have you.<br /> <br /> When making generic enemies like these, I sometimes don't even bother to write down their stats, I'll just decide (I think this guy would roll 4 dice) and just keep it consistent. If they have special abilities then I'll make a note of that, but for the most part I'll just roll a suitable seeming amount of dice as and when the encounter happens.<br /> If the players are getting too hurt too fast and I roll well, I'll describe the roll as Bashing damage, saving the bulk of the Lethal to mages capable of healing themselves.<br /> If the players start to relax a bit too much because things are a little too easy, then I'll adapt to that.<br /> <br /> In many ways, I'm giving them the illusion of danger without ever actually have them in threat of death.<br /> <br /> That being said, I never protect them from failure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T10:07:12-08:00","id":1024804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1023864-limits-on-sustaining-locking-and-other-preparation?p=1024772#post1024772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You may not like my way of doing things, but I don't really worry about fully stating up my NPCs. For important ones, I might note down what spheres I expect them to all have, their arete level, and maybe their attributes, just so I keep a little consistency, but that's about it. Everything else is really free-form.<br /> For example, when my players are fighting spirits, I'll have a few spirits prepared, and just throw 2 at them and see how they get on. If they're having a lot of trouble with them, then I'll leave it at that. If they seem to tear through them pretty easily, I'll add a couple more mid-battle.<br /> <br /> The same thing can be done with the NWO Blacksuits, Progentior Clones/Victors, Demons, Nephandic goons, thugs, what have you.<br /> <br /> When making generic enemies like these, I sometimes don't even bother to write down their stats, I'll just decide (I think this guy would roll 4 dice) and just keep it consistent. If they have special abilities then I'll make a note of that, but for the most part I'll just roll a suitable seeming amount of dice as and when the encounter happens.<br /> If the players are getting too hurt too fast and I roll well, I'll describe the roll as Bashing damage, saving the bulk of the Lethal to mages capable of healing themselves.<br /> If the players start to relax a bit too much because things are a little too easy, then I'll adapt to that.<br /> <br /> In many ways, I'm giving them the illusion of danger without ever actually have them in threat of death.<br /> <br /> That being said, I never protect them from failure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sort of the same as I wanted to convey.<br /> But more elaborate und clear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}